WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.727
This query checks email shape.

00:00:01.727 --> 00:00:04.457
Missing values receive a missing status.

00:00:04.457 --> 00:00:08.927
Values matching the teaching-level regular expression are labeled valid shape.

00:00:08.927 --> 00:00:12.077
Other nonmissing values are flagged for review.

00:00:12.077 --> 00:00:17.412
The phrase valid shape is important because the regex does not prove the mailbox exists.

00:00:17.412 --> 00:00:22.052
Standardization should make equivalent values comparable without inventing facts.

00:00:22.052 --> 00:00:29.637
Lowercasing an email or normalizing a known category map is different from guessing what an ambiguous value

00:00:29.637 --> 00:00:33.691
was supposed to mean. Good cleaning reduces representation noise while preserving uncertainty.
